From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:52:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: offer the setup wizard after a reinstall over stock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Return to Flashforge firmware keeps Kiln's data, and with it the
screen's settings, where the setup wizard is marked done; a reinstall
from the install stick went straight to the home screen. The installer
now leaves HELIX_WIZARD_OFFER_FILE (S70helixscreen:
/data/ad5x/helixscreen/offer-setup-wizard) when it finds those
settings. At the next start, when no wizard runs, the screen asks
"Run the setup wizard?" once: Run deletes the file and opens the same
session as Settings > Printer > Run Setup Wizard (refused with a toast
while a print may move the printer; the file stays), Skip deletes it
and stays home, a dismissal keeps it for the next start. A wizard
running at that start anyway, or a SETUP_WIZARD from Klipper while the
question is up, answers it: the file goes, the question closes.
Nothing happens without the variable. The two new texts are in en.yml
and in every other language file: Run and Skip are existing keys that
all of them translate, so a language with only the buttons would show
an English question above them. The Russian uses the printer terms of
the other Kiln strings (мастер настройки, филамент, смещение по Z,
прошивку плат); the others use each file's own words for the setup wizard, the
Z offset and the controller boards. Korean and Turkish also get the
existing key "Cannot calibrate while printing" (Run's toast during a
print), which they lacked. Tests in test_kiln_wizard_offer.cpp, in
Russian and in German.

Upstream: not applicable (Kiln OS specific)
